        },
        "subject": "LU-0000 lov: fix page ref leak in EC recovery",
        "message": "LU-0000 lov: fix page ref leak in EC recovery\n\nlov_ec_read_stripe_pages() calls grab_cache_page() taking a reference\nto the data page in addition to taking a cl_page reference. But the\ncleanup in lov_io_ec_rd_start() only releases the ref for\nEC_DPG_UPTODATE pages. The reference on EC_DPG_READ and EC_DPG_ERROR\npages is leaked, so reconstructed pages cannot be freed at unlink and\naccumulate orphaned on the file LRU.\n\nThis fix releases the ref for EC_DPG_READ/EC_DPG_ERROR pages in both\ncleanup paths (rg_cleanup and out). This is similar to how\nll_read_ahead_page() handles it.\n\nTest-Parameters: forjanitoronly\nSigned-off-by: Marc Vef <mvef@whamcloud.com>\nChange-Id: I2d7b9e644f26367567dea5f5317e191afa5eadc6\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
